{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none. The model contains no observed data likelihood; `N`, `ts`, and `x_left` are context inputs only and are not scored by sampling statements.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The only sampling statement is the built-in prior `xs_forward_ncp ~ normal(0, 1)` for the top-level parameter, and there are no protected observations or forbidden manual log-density operations.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  array[N] real ts;

  real x_left;
}

parameters {
  array[N - 1] real xs_forward_ncp;
}

transformed parameters {
  array[N] real xs;

  xs[1] = x_left;

  for (n in 2:N) {
    xs[n]
      = xs[n - 1] + sqrt(ts[n] - ts[n - 1]) * xs_forward_ncp[n - 1];
  }
}

model {
  xs_forward_ncp ~ normal(0, 1);
}

","data_safe_json":"{"N": 3, "ts": [1.0, 2.0, 3.0], "x_left": 5.478387009757785}","protected_variables":[]}
